{title: BLUEBERRY HILL}
{subtitle: Fats Domino}
   On the bass strings:  Form up (G) and pick the notes indicated on strings 6, 5, and 4 before moving to (C).

   On the trebel strings (which emulates the pitch of the piano in the recording):  Form up (C) and lift off the index finger to get to (Cmaj7).  Pick the notes indicated on strings 3 and 2, dropping your pinky onto the note <d> at the 2nd string/3rd fret - lift off, replace, and then strum (CaddG) which is just (C) with your finger add to note <g> on the 3rd string/1st fret.  Then just lift off to get back to (C).

   If transposing, play the transposed root note, adding the 5th note as necessary.  Notes may or many not transpose.

